course: dictionary
lesson: 12838
title: Encircle: a ring around something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To encircle something is to form a circle round it, or to surround it on all sides. Think of a ring: a ring encircles your finger. When you meet this word, look for clues that show a ring, a wall, or a shape going all the way round.
explain: «Tall mountains encircle the green valley.» The mountains are not on just one side. They go all the way round, so the valley sits inside a ring of mountains. Encircled is the past form, as in «The lake was encircled by trees.»
explain: In history, encircle has a stronger meaning. «The soldiers encircled the city, so no food could get in or out.» Here, encircle means to surround a place so that nobody can get in or out. The clues are the words no food and in or out.
fact: To encircle means to form a circle round something, or to surround it on all sides.
fact: In war, to encircle a place means to surround it so nobody can get in or out.
fact: Encircle is a verb. Its other forms are encircles, encircled and encircling.
fact: «The children encircled the lost puppy» means they stood in a ring around it.
fact: Encircled is often used with by: «The town was encircled by hills.»
fact: Surround is a close synonym of encircle, but encircle suggests a circle or ring shape.
exercise: «The lake is encircled by trees.» What does encircled mean here? | Covered in thick snow | Pushed far away from the land | *Surrounded on all sides, like a ring | Drained of all its water
exercise: «The soldiers encircled the castle.» What does encircle mean in this sentence? | Paint a circle on the castle wall | Build a brand new castle | Visit the castle for one day | *Surround the castle so nobody can get in or out
exercise: Find and copy the word that means make a ring round: «Tall mountains encircle the green valley.» | tall | green | *encircle | valley
test: «A ring of lights encircled the old tower.» What does encircled mean? | *Surrounded the tower in a ring | Turned the tower off for the night | Painted the tower bright red | Knocked the tower down
test: Ella says encircle means to dig a hole. Is she right? | No, it means to fly high in the sky | *No, it means to surround something, like a ring | Yes, it means to dig a hole and fill it in | Yes, it means to sit down quietly
exam: «Wolves encircled the sheep, and the sheep could not run away.» What does encircled mean here? | Fed with food and water | *Surrounded on every side | Scattered far apart across the field | Stared at for a long time
